column40:
MS (pencil) notes on second rear free end-paper recto: "Not Geo Steevens’ copy wh was sold in 1800 / and purchased by Geo Daniel / and was again sold at the Daniel / sale in 1864. / But Richd Farmer copy / Lot 7930 in his sale 1798 / sold for £8--. "; 

Sold by Mr. Thomas King at the sale of the library of the late Revd. Richard Farmer (1735-1797)(Bibliotheca Farmeriana) in May-June, 1798 (lot 7930). From the catalogue entry: "The MS at the end has been thought to be Shakespeare's autograph." UML copy of catalogue is marked up with the sale price of £8.;

From the collection of George John, 2nd Earl Spencer (1758-1834).

Furness, Horace Howard (bookplate) (inscription);
Halliwell-Phillipps, J. O. (James Orchard), 1820-1889 (autograph, 2 January 1871); 
Furness, Horace Howard, Jr. (donor); 
Furness, Louise Brooks Winsor (donor)
